      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-68028",
      ":question/problem": "There is a proportional relationship between the volume of gas $v$ (in liters) that a bus uses and the distance $d$ (in kilometers) that it travels.\n\n| Liters ($v$) | Kilometers ($d$) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ | $12$ |\n| $4$ | $48$ |\n| $8$ | $96$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The bus drives $1$ kilometer using $12$ liters of gas.\n2. The unit rate is $12$ kilometers per liter.\n3. If the bus uses $3$ liters of gas it will travel $30$ kilometers."
    },
