      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-91946",
      ":question/problem": "The following table shows a proportional relationship between the weight $w$ (in kilograms) of detergent purchased at a particular supermarket and the total cost $c$ (in dollars) that customers must pay.\n\n| Weight ($w$) | Cost ($c$) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $3$ | $4.5$ |\n| $6$ | $9$ |\n| $8$ | $12$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The unit rate is $$3$ per kilogram.\n2. One kilogram of detergent costs $$1.25$.\n3. The cost of $10$ kilograms of powder is $$15$."
    }
